# A policy per path, not a list of what happened to be untracked (issue #3380).
#
# certs/ has no rule on purpose. Every file under it is published evidence:
# verify/certify_all.py and verify/heuristic_certify.py write there by design,
# verify/check_certs.py refuses a certificate that claims a level it lacks, and
# verify/check_tree_consistency.py refuses one that outlives its entry. A
# certificate is added deliberately, in a PR; nothing under certs/ is scratch.

# Python and environments
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv*/

# `_`-prefixed scratch scripts (e.g. research/_find_dominators.py, verify/_sweep_ub.py)
_*.py
_finalize.*
_foldcerts.*
*.log

# Working output under research/. Stage finds under research/candidates/, put
# run output under research/out/ or research/runs/; these are the directories
# verify/check_prose.py refuses as evidence. Anything else under research/ is
# meant to be committed.
research/candidates/
research/out/
research/runs/
research/board*.json
# Advisory cell claims (qldpc targets --claim): per-second, advisory, and
# worthless once expired, so committing them would only guarantee a merge
# conflict on every branch that claims anything.
research/claims/

# Under repro/ the tree holds one manifest per entry, repro/<slug>.json. A
# working directory beside it (run output, receipts, exported matrices) is
# what two submission PRs committed with `git add -A` (issue #3810); the
# scope check refuses it on a submission PR, and this keeps it out of the
# index in the first place. Directories already tracked stay tracked.
repro/*/

# Agent-harness scaffolding: draft PR bodies and exported session transcripts.
# AGENTS.md requires the scaffolding deleted before review, so none of it
# belongs in the tree.
.prs/
.pr-body-*.md
session-ses_*.md
# machine-local agent configuration (absolute paths into one home directory)
opencode.json

# LaTeX build artifacts (talks/, docs/); the .tex/.bib sources and .pdf outputs are tracked
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.out
# compiled gf2 accelerator
*.so
build/
# downloaded packages
*.deb
# macOS folder metadata
.DS_Store
# conference / paper material lives outside this repo (issue #325)
talks/
